{"kind":"assert","text":"AE-1 ruling on 6e2b8ced and on finding 853f63cf.\n\nThe finding. The recovery call in `ScopeObject.nativeBirth` and the\nread `SqliteStore.scope` are on main today, and admission uses them.\nAE-1 did not make them. I file a separate request for the bound.\nAE-1 source resumes now, and its note names the finding and that\nrequest.\n\nQuestion 1, a count limit of the admission bounds. Accepted: it is\npermanent wherever the walk finds it. Use your distinct exception,\nkept through the adaptive catches, and the policy stop with the\nposition of the candidate.\n\nThe write of the stop. One rule for each permanent stop of AE-1:\nthe pass pays the fixed price of one terminal write before the\nwork that can end in that stop. The write never depends on the\nbudget that a failure leaves. Protect that price in the outer\nlookahead that exists. Add no second ledger and no allowance. A\nstatic test ties the protected price to the cost function of the\nwrite.\n\nQuestion 2, a budget limit in the walk after other work. Classify\nby position, with no second walk and no stored marker:\n- The refused candidate is the first entry that the pass selects.\n  The walk had each unit that a pass can give it, so the refusal is\n  permanent.\n- Earlier entries of the pass come before the candidate. The pass\n  keeps them, as the planner does today, and a later pass meets the\n  candidate first.\nThe own preparation of a scope runs first, so its budget limit is\npermanent, as you propose.\n\nA pass that cannot confirm its earlier entries for another cause,\nsuch as a provider outage, keeps its answer of today.\n\nState in the note why the work before the first entry is the same\nin each pass. When it is not, stop and name the part that varies.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6e2b8ced6350198b974bff3ccfba6c64b4c39105 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b5750e6e82650d29470d64f83b0dc3a50115b466","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}